-- title:
--   Lower bound m^t for the toric m-torsion subgroup
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $N_0 \ne 0$, with $p$ prime and nonzero, and assume $p \nmid N_0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of a fixed algebraic closure $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ of $\mathbf Q$ lying over $p$, in the sense that $p$ is a nonunit of $A$, and let $\Lambda$ be level data for $N_0, p, A$: a section $\sigma_A$ from $\operatorname{Spec} A$ to the base over which the generic point factors as prescribed, a scheme $X$ over that base carrying a relative group law, together with bijections identifying $J^0(N_0)$ with the points of $X$ over the generic point and the analogous group over the residue field of $A$ with the points of $X$ over the special point. Let $O$ be a Néron object of level $N_0 p$ over these data: a scheme $G$ over the base, equipped with a commutative relative group law, a bijection $\mathrm{pts}$ between $J^0(N_0 p)$ and the points of $G$ over the generic point that is additive, Galois-equivariant and compatible with an action of the Hecke algebra $\mathbf Z[T_\ell]$ through endomorphisms over the base, with $G \to \operatorname{Spec}$ of the base smooth, separated, locally of finite type, quasi-compact, surjective with preconnected fibres, multiplication by each $n > 0$ flat and surjective, proper generic fibre, a toric rank $\mathrm{toricRank} \in \mathbf N$ and the remaining fields of the structure (summarised here). Let $m$ be a natural number with $0 < m$. The assertion is that $m^{\mathrm{toricRank}}$ is at most the cardinality of $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$, the subgroup of $J^0(N_0 p)$ generated by the image of the family $O.\mathrm{toricPoint}\,m$.
--
--   This is the elementary half of the computation of the toric part of the $m$-torsion of the semistable Jacobian at $p$: the torus $\mu_{m,A}^{t}$ sitting inside the Néron object contributes at least $m^{t}$ points, $t$ being the toric rank. It is used in the determination of the cardinality of the toric $m$-torsion and in the comparison of `toricPts` with `finPts` that separates the toric from the abelian part of the special fibre.
-- source:
